WEBVTT

01:45.500 --> 01:50.500
<b>Heart and Reason</b>

01:47.370 --> 01:51.000
He eats so much. It's great.

01:51.000 --> 01:53.750
Grow up strong, Rokurota.

01:55.760 --> 01:58.840
Oh, my. Is it playtime 
now that he's had a snack?

02:18.400 --> 02:20.240
Stand back, Sagiri!

02:33.130 --> 02:34.460
Genji-dono!

02:38.170 --> 02:39.630
You need immediate medical attention.

02:40.050 --> 02:42.720
Run, Sagiri.

02:43.760 --> 02:45.260
It's too late for me.

02:46.680 --> 02:49.520
Hurry... run...

03:04.160 --> 03:05.370
Gabimaru...

03:05.370 --> 03:09.790
Is he a condemned criminal or a monster?

03:10.460 --> 03:12.250
He's practically unharmed.

03:12.540 --> 03:16.920
That's Rokurota, the Giant of Bizen.

03:17.250 --> 03:19.050
He's assigned to...

03:20.970 --> 03:22.380
Eizen-dono.

03:26.260 --> 03:28.970
<i>Those are the eyes 
of a predator who's located his prey.</i>

03:29.560 --> 03:32.190
<i>It'll be tough for us to escape together.</i>

03:33.190 --> 03:34.480
Then I have no choice.

03:35.310 --> 03:36.570
I'll kill him.

03:37.650 --> 03:39.570
<i>That said, how?</i>

03:39.860 --> 03:44.570
<i>If that kick was ineffective, 
then he's as tough as an Iwagakure.</i>

03:45.530 --> 03:48.830
Shinobi Rule Number Nine.

03:48.830 --> 03:53.120
<i>Accurately analyze the enemy's abilities.</i>

03:54.040 --> 03:56.460
<i>I'll decide once I see how strong he is.</i>

04:02.720 --> 04:03.970
What?

04:13.480 --> 04:15.150
Stay back. You'll die.

04:15.440 --> 04:16.520
But...

04:17.190 --> 04:19.020
<i>Physically, he's stronger than me.</i>

04:19.400 --> 04:21.900
How long are you going to 
sit there and watch, Yuzuriha?

04:22.360 --> 04:23.400
Help me.

04:23.650 --> 04:25.740
You've got your own ninjutsu, don't you?

04:25.740 --> 04:27.780
Fight with me, like you promised you would.

04:27.780 --> 04:29.490
Okay, okay.

04:29.490 --> 04:31.290
Of course I'll keep my promises.

04:33.040 --> 04:34.580
You're responsible for the fighting,

04:34.580 --> 04:36.670
and I'm responsible 
for gathering information.

04:37.540 --> 04:39.250
You've got this, Gabimaru.

04:39.250 --> 04:41.050
Don't let him beat you, Gabimaru.

04:41.050 --> 04:42.920
Go, go. Get him.

04:42.920 --> 04:44.720
You're so strong, Gabimaru.

04:44.720 --> 04:46.050
Get out there.

04:48.600 --> 04:50.310
<i>There's nothing special about his swings.</i>

04:50.310 --> 04:52.680
<i>If I just focus on the 
destruction wrought by his fists...</i>

05:02.900 --> 05:04.990
<i>His swings and reactions are fast.</i>

05:05.360 --> 05:07.280
<i>I can feel it instinctively.</i>

05:07.610 --> 05:09.330
<i>It's impossible to defend 
against those fists.</i>

05:09.330 --> 05:10.660
<i>Touching them would mean instant death.</i>

05:10.990 --> 05:11.790
<i>In that case...</i>

05:12.410 --> 05:14.620
Ninpo: Stone Storm.

05:24.800 --> 05:27.050
<i>Projectiles are ineffective.</i>

05:29.930 --> 05:31.560
<i>Ninpo: Unformed Blade.</i>

05:34.180 --> 05:37.190
<i>Not even my Unformed Blade, which is 
comparable to steel, works against him.</i>

05:34.220 --> 05:37.940
<b>Ninpo: Unformed Blade</b>

05:38.600 --> 05:40.150
<b>Ninpo:
Savage
 Headbutt</b>

05:39.610 --> 05:40.940
<i>What else do I have?</i>

05:39.610 --> 05:41.110
<b>Ninpo:
Aqueous
 Bomb</b>

05:39.900 --> 05:41.360
<b>Ninpo:
Quilt of
 Thorns</b>

05:40.360 --> 05:41.860
<b>Ninpo:
Savage
Headbutt</b>

05:41.110 --> 05:42.610
<b>Ninpo:
Zephyr
 Weave</b>

05:41.270 --> 05:44.190
<i>What long-range ninjutsu 
would be effective against him?</i>

05:41.860 --> 05:43.360
<b>Ninpo:
Wild
Archer</b>

05:42.360 --> 05:43.860
<b>Ninpo:
Savage
 Headbutt</b>

05:46.740 --> 05:48.070
Enough.

05:48.490 --> 05:49.820
This is pointless.

05:50.410 --> 05:54.080
Run, Sagiri.

05:54.080 --> 05:55.830
Don't give up.

05:55.830 --> 05:58.330
You'll survive if we can stop the bleeding.

05:59.120 --> 06:01.170
You're a strange person.

06:02.170 --> 06:06.470
Moments ago, you were blustering like a man.

06:07.840 --> 06:11.100
But now, I feel a woman's affection in you.

06:11.100 --> 06:13.470
Right now, there are no men or women.

06:13.470 --> 06:16.560
I simply don't want my senior, who 
studied under the same master to die.

06:21.400 --> 06:24.020
So that's how you've chosen to live.

06:25.150 --> 06:29.530
Rather than dividing everything in two, 
such as man or woman, strength or weakness,

06:30.070 --> 06:33.870
you accept opposing 
concepts as part of yourself.

06:34.370 --> 06:36.620
You embody the middle way.

06:36.620 --> 06:38.870
That is your conviction.

06:40.170 --> 06:43.250
I finally understand.

06:46.210 --> 06:48.590
A warrior's sword is his soul.

06:49.260 --> 06:51.340
I give this to you.

06:52.390 --> 06:56.930
Rokurota probably killed Eizen-dono.

07:00.560 --> 07:05.650
If you're a samurai, then I won't
 tell you to run anymore.

07:06.900 --> 07:09.650
Kill Rokurota,

07:11.530 --> 07:15.030
Yamada Asaemon Sagiri.

07:20.540 --> 07:24.000
<i>Close-quarters combat is too dangerous. 
Projectiles are ineffective.</i>

07:25.040 --> 07:27.300
<i>If I could just get the chance 
to use Ascetic Blaze...</i>

07:31.970 --> 07:35.350
<i>If it were two against one, 
I could find a blind spot.</i>

07:39.850 --> 07:44.730
If you insert your blade at the junction 
of extended muscles, tendons, and bone,

07:45.310 --> 07:47.730
even the strongest body can be cut.

07:47.730 --> 07:52.490
No matter how outlandish your opponent, 
the principles of execution apply.

07:52.490 --> 07:56.080
Understand the structure of their body 
and strike at the gaps.

07:56.830 --> 07:59.950
That is the Yamada Asaemon style.

08:01.500 --> 08:02.540
Gabimaru.

08:03.000 --> 08:06.250
Good timing. I was just looking for help.

08:07.210 --> 08:08.750
Assist me.

08:09.800 --> 08:13.340
Um, I'd like to go tend 
my fellow student's wounds.

08:13.340 --> 08:16.140
What? But it's too late for him.

08:16.510 --> 08:20.020
Besides, you're not 
that kind of guy, are you?

08:21.390 --> 08:26.150
More importantly, no monsters have 
approached despite the noise we're making.

08:26.440 --> 08:29.070
Wouldn't it be more beneficial 
to observe them?

08:29.400 --> 08:33.320
We can flee once they're dead.

08:33.990 --> 08:35.950
His bleeding has stopped already.

08:36.280 --> 08:39.790
So that wasn't a serious injury for him.

08:40.120 --> 08:42.080
We need a single killing blow.

08:42.080 --> 08:44.370
We'll have to aim for the gaps 
between his bones and decapitate him.

08:44.750 --> 08:46.880
But his neck is too high up.

08:47.290 --> 08:49.090
So we'll split up.

08:49.460 --> 08:51.920
Cut his legs from his blind spot 
and make him kneel.

08:52.260 --> 08:53.920
You say that so casually.

08:53.920 --> 08:54.880
Huh?

08:56.090 --> 08:58.260
You can do it, can't you?

09:01.220 --> 09:02.980
I'll handle his attacks.

09:14.780 --> 09:15.400
What?

09:21.740 --> 09:22.950
Are you all right?

09:22.950 --> 09:24.040
Yes.

09:24.750 --> 09:28.130
<i>He's condemned to death 
and killed my senior.</i>

09:30.170 --> 09:33.550
<i>But if I attack too aggressively, 
my swordsmanship will suffer.</i>

09:34.170 --> 09:35.510
<i>I must remain calm.</i>

09:35.880 --> 09:38.930
<i>I must push aside my emotions 
and rely on reason.</i>

09:42.180 --> 09:44.060
He's coming. Again.

09:47.900 --> 09:49.400
<i>My leg...</i>

09:49.400 --> 09:51.860
<i>I must've strained it 
while evading his blows.</i>

09:52.190 --> 09:54.440
<i>Dodging all his attacks takes 
a high degree of skill.</i>

09:55.070 --> 09:57.400
<i>A simple open-palm strike 
from him hits like a cannon.</i>

09:57.740 --> 09:59.280
<i>I must remain calm.</i>

09:59.280 --> 10:01.160
<i>If I'm struck by a single blow, it's over.</i>

10:05.370 --> 10:08.790
Cutting through his bones 
while he's rampaging about will be difficult.

10:08.790 --> 10:11.960
His movements close the gaps between his 
bones, leaving no space for my blade.

10:12.090 --> 10:15.880
Normally, beheadings are performed 
on people bowing their heads.

10:15.880 --> 10:19.090
Killing him with a single blow 
requires him to hunch over.

10:19.340 --> 10:22.100
But since our blades 
can't penetrate his limbs,

10:22.100 --> 10:25.600
it'll be difficult to make him do that.

10:27.520 --> 10:29.440
This is a tough problem.

10:32.770 --> 10:35.070
Is his stomach growling?

10:40.910 --> 10:42.490
What is this?

10:43.990 --> 10:45.450
He's so loud.

10:58.300 --> 10:59.260
Gabimaru!

11:03.100 --> 11:08.520
<i>His extraordinary strength made me 
cautious, but I can withstand this.</i>

11:08.890 --> 11:10.560
<i>I can handle this.</i>

11:15.480 --> 11:16.780
No!

11:18.990 --> 11:21.910
<i>Crap. I need to get back up.</i>

11:21.910 --> 11:23.370
<i>That wasn't a fatal blow.</i>

11:23.370 --> 11:24.780
<i>Stand up.</i>

11:31.290 --> 11:32.250
<i>Death.</i>

11:33.290 --> 11:36.500
<i>Calm down. I must remain calm.</i>

11:36.880 --> 11:40.010
<i>Suppress your emotions. Think logically.</i>

11:40.420 --> 11:41.720
<i>Calm down.</i>

11:41.720 --> 11:45.010
<i>Abandon your passion and remain calm.</i>

11:45.010 --> 11:48.890
The middle way. That is your conviction.

11:49.390 --> 11:55.480
<i>Rather than dividing everything in two, 
accept the opposing concepts as they are.</i>

11:58.280 --> 12:00.650
<i>Both emotion and reason.</i>

12:14.710 --> 12:16.880
<i>Turn your emotions into strength.</i>

12:16.880 --> 12:19.300
<i>Use logic to keep sight of the objective.</i>

12:19.300 --> 12:21.800
<i>Choose neither calmness nor passion,</i>

12:22.680 --> 12:23.800
<i>but the middle.</i>

12:30.270 --> 12:31.640
Wow.

12:31.640 --> 12:35.310
Her Tameshi-itto-ryu rank is 12th,

12:35.310 --> 12:39.400
but Yamada clan ranks 
aren't determined by pure skill alone.

12:39.860 --> 12:43.200
They're assigned according 
to their suitability to lead the clan,

12:43.200 --> 12:45.860
so she loses standing simply 
for being a woman.

12:45.860 --> 12:49.410
In terms of pure skill, she's...

12:49.870 --> 12:53.870
<i>Sagiri lacks experience 
as a warrior on the battlefield.</i>

12:54.250 --> 12:59.380
<i>But when her duty and goals 
are aligned with her heart,</i>

12:59.800 --> 13:01.380
<i>when her hesitation vanishes,</i>

13:02.090 --> 13:05.260
<i>her skill with a sword 
is better than first-rate.</i>

13:08.640 --> 13:11.890
She may fear the monsters of the island,

13:11.890 --> 13:17.020
but as an Asaemon, in the face 
of a criminal, she shows no fear.

13:18.440 --> 13:20.900
She's one stubborn person.

13:21.230 --> 13:23.990
<i>I was right about her.</i>

13:24.400 --> 13:26.410
<i>That feeling I got when I first met her...</i>

13:26.860 --> 13:29.580
<i>She's strong.</i>

13:36.920 --> 13:40.920
<i>A low-hanging head...</i>

13:51.890 --> 13:54.180
I guess it's not that simple.

13:54.180 --> 13:57.520
Is there any way to keep his head bowed?

13:58.440 --> 13:59.900
I've got an idea.

13:59.900 --> 14:00.860
What?

14:01.270 --> 14:03.230
It might be a bit extreme.

14:09.990 --> 14:11.830
<i>The Giant of Bizen.</i>

14:11.830 --> 14:15.410
<i>Close-quarters combat is too dangerous. 
Projectiles are ineffective.</i>

14:16.160 --> 14:19.790
<i>Our only option is to get a blade through 
a gap in his body and decapitate him.</i>

14:20.880 --> 14:24.130
<i>Doing that requires more than 
exceptional physical abilities.</i>

14:25.170 --> 14:29.300
<i>We need the skills of the Yamada 
Asaemon clan, specialized in beheading.</i>

14:31.430 --> 14:33.720
<i>But given his massive bulk 
and reaction speed,</i>

14:33.720 --> 14:36.020
<i>a half-hearted effort won't be enough 
to reach him with a blade.</i>

14:36.230 --> 14:37.230
<i>In that case...</i>

14:44.230 --> 14:45.030
Crap.

14:45.030 --> 14:45.900
What?

14:45.900 --> 14:47.530
We're getting out of here, Senta.

14:47.900 --> 14:51.280
<i>Ninpo: Stone Storm, Ascetic Blaze Mode.</i>

14:54.410 --> 14:57.500
<i>Ninpo: Zephyr Weave, Ascetic Blaze Mode.</i>

14:58.160 --> 15:00.750
<i>Ninpo: Grand Crag, Ascetic Blaze Mode.</i>

15:02.540 --> 15:05.800
<i>Ninpo: Quilt of Thorns, Ascetic Blaze Mode.</i>

15:15.010 --> 15:16.890
Any more would be reckless.

15:17.350 --> 15:20.140
Besides, this should be enough.

15:25.270 --> 15:27.150
How far do we need to run?

15:27.150 --> 15:29.570
As far as we can, you four-eyed raccoon dog.

15:29.570 --> 15:32.570
They're not just trying to kill Rokurota.

15:33.030 --> 15:35.280
They're planning to set 
the whole area on fire.

15:36.910 --> 15:38.160
Could it be?

15:38.160 --> 15:39.040
It's the smoke.

15:39.040 --> 15:41.670
The massive amount of smoke 
produced by the oils in raw wood.

15:41.670 --> 15:45.090
By setting fire to branches and leaves,

15:45.090 --> 15:48.510
they can instantly fill the area above 
with smoke, given smoke's properties.

15:48.510 --> 15:50.170
And if he rampages about while crying,

15:50.170 --> 15:52.930
he'll run short of breath 
and inhale a large amount of smoke.

15:54.510 --> 15:55.800
Like execution by fire,

15:56.220 --> 15:58.390
the poison in the smoke 
that causes loss of consciousness

15:58.390 --> 16:01.140
when inhaled is more harmful 
than the flames or heat.

16:01.140 --> 16:02.060
Poison?

16:02.060 --> 16:04.560
<i>In other words, carbon monoxide.</i>

16:04.810 --> 16:07.440
<i>It binds to the hemoglobin in the blood,</i>

16:07.440 --> 16:11.280
<i>causing the entire body to rapidly reach 
an oxygen deficient state.</i>

16:11.280 --> 16:14.200
<i>It is known as carbon monoxide poisoning.</i>

16:14.620 --> 16:16.530
That was tough for me too,

16:16.530 --> 16:18.910
but as long as you stay crouched, 
you won't inhale any smoke.

16:18.910 --> 16:20.250
It's safe.

16:20.250 --> 16:21.830
I could burn to death.

16:23.580 --> 16:25.670
Will he reach his limit first?

16:25.670 --> 16:28.670
Or will his head come down first?

16:49.530 --> 16:51.110
Cut him now while we have the chance!

16:51.110 --> 16:53.110
I won't last long in a contest of strength!

17:01.950 --> 17:03.250
<i>Calmly.</i>

17:05.580 --> 17:06.710
<i>Fiercely.</i>

17:22.020 --> 17:23.730
<i>Hungry.</i>

17:22.600 --> 17:23.980
<i>Wanna play.</i>

17:23.980 --> 17:25.560
<i>Wanna play. Wanna play.</i>

17:25.560 --> 17:29.230
<i>Hungry. Hungry.</i>

17:29.610 --> 17:32.610
<i>Why don't I ever feel full?</i>

17:32.610 --> 17:35.150
<i>Why won't anyone play with me?</i>

17:36.950 --> 17:39.740
We allowed you to go on quite a rampage.

17:40.200 --> 17:43.620
We must've frightened you. I'm sorry.

17:43.620 --> 17:45.710
It's my fault for lacking experience.

17:47.920 --> 17:49.590
But it's all right now.

17:50.290 --> 17:52.760
Nobody hates you.

17:53.130 --> 17:55.420
Those who might hate you now are dead.

17:57.260 --> 18:02.060
Like them, I hope you rest in peace.

18:07.270 --> 18:09.270
The flames are getting stronger.

18:09.650 --> 18:11.690
Monsters might approach.

18:11.690 --> 18:13.530
We should get away from here.

18:21.780 --> 18:22.990
Genji-dono...

18:23.790 --> 18:26.410
If we don't hurry, we'll burn to death.

18:36.010 --> 18:40.220
<i>On this island where I can't mourn my 
fellow students, much less criminals,</i>

18:40.930 --> 18:43.930
<i>I must be strong.</i>

18:47.060 --> 18:48.270
<i>Strong...</i>

18:50.190 --> 18:52.270
<i>Rather than dividing everything in two,</i>

18:52.270 --> 18:54.610
<i>such as strength or weakness, 
you accept them.</i>

18:55.190 --> 18:57.900
<i>That is your conviction.</i>

19:10.870 --> 19:12.630
They're coming.

19:12.630 --> 19:15.210
They're heading toward the flames.

19:15.710 --> 19:20.220
But normally, animals instinctively avoid fire.

19:20.680 --> 19:23.720
They're looking less and less natural.

19:25.810 --> 19:27.310
We don't have a choice.

19:27.310 --> 19:29.850
Let's head in the direction 
where the monsters came from.

19:29.850 --> 19:31.100
Wouldn't that be dangerous?

19:31.480 --> 19:34.860
Well, yeah, but we have no other choice.

19:34.860 --> 19:38.440
The monsters' ecology 
is our only lead on the Elixir.

19:39.360 --> 19:42.530
I'm still feeling the damage I took earlier.

19:42.530 --> 19:45.280
I need a break. This is such a pain.

19:46.450 --> 19:47.700
Would you rather give up, then?

19:47.700 --> 19:48.830
No.

19:49.120 --> 19:53.330
No matter how small or dangerous, 
if it's a lead, I'll follow it.

19:53.330 --> 19:57.960
I'll find the Elixir of Life as quickly as 
possible and see my wife as soon as I can.

19:58.920 --> 20:02.970
Are you sure you're not worried about 
the safety of your fellow students?

20:07.770 --> 20:08.470
No.

20:09.060 --> 20:12.230
They all took this job 
knowing it could kill them.

20:12.730 --> 20:14.980
It would be disrespectful 
to be too concerned about them.

20:15.900 --> 20:17.360
If I'm worried about my fellows,

20:17.360 --> 20:20.110
then I should find 
the Elixir as quickly as possible

20:20.110 --> 20:22.860
and release us from this responsibility.

20:24.870 --> 20:26.740
Our interests are finally aligned.

20:27.120 --> 20:29.620
I'm still your monitor.

20:37.420 --> 20:38.460
What is that?

20:38.880 --> 20:42.680
The vixen and raccoon 
dog fled all the way here?

20:47.600 --> 20:51.230
Hey, what about our promise 
to fight together?

20:53.690 --> 20:58.110
Is this a village?

20:59.530 --> 21:01.860
Doesn't look like it could be anything else.

21:02.570 --> 21:06.490
If this place really is Shinsenkyo,

21:06.780 --> 21:10.370
does that mean hermits live in this village?

21:24.470 --> 21:25.970
Man, that's gross.

21:25.970 --> 21:28.180
Doesn't even fill you up.

21:28.180 --> 21:31.520
Is that safe to eat?

21:31.520 --> 21:34.100
I'm not eating it, I'm drinking it.

21:34.100 --> 21:37.400
The bodily fluids of animals are the 
water you drink in the mountains.

21:39.690 --> 21:44.950
Anyway, what are those 
hermits you mentioned earlier?

21:44.950 --> 21:48.030
Well... they're imaginary.

21:48.320 --> 21:51.450
They're a type of superhuman being 
according to Shenxian philosophy.

21:51.450 --> 21:54.960
Most resemble old men 
and cast mysterious spells.

21:54.960 --> 21:56.670
Allegedly, they're immortal.

21:56.790 --> 21:59.540
They may exist on this island.

21:59.540 --> 22:04.550
It's supposed to be hermits, 
not monsters, that live in Shinsenkyo.

22:04.840 --> 22:06.930
Sounds dumb.

22:06.930 --> 22:09.350
Just kill the old farts and be done with it.

22:09.350 --> 22:11.560
They might actually satisfy my hunger.

22:12.640 --> 22:14.060
You're joking, right?

22:17.480 --> 22:18.440
Brother?

22:18.810 --> 22:20.900
Something's out there.

22:23.070 --> 22:25.570
These better be good.
